Article 5 (Dismissal of Members) The Minister of Health and Welfare may dismiss a Committee member from commission if the member falls under any of the following cases:
1. Where the member becomes unable to perform duties for a prolonged period due to physical or mental weakness, etc.;
2. Where the member violates the duty of confidentiality under Article 13;
3. Where the member has engaged in misconduct in connection with duties;
4. Where the member is deemed unfit to serve as a member due to neglect of duties, conduct damaging dignity, or other grounds;
5. Where the member states that he or she is unable to perform the duties of a member.
